{"nodes": [{"id": "contributing_tests_prove_behaviour", "label": "Tests prove behaviour, not coverage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A test that would not have caught a real defect is not worth the maintenance; the suite already caught three genuine bugs and that is the bar."}, {"id": "contributing_comments_explain_why", "label": "Comments explain why, never what", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The code says what it does; a comment earns its place by recording a decision, a constraint or a trap."}, {"id": "contributing_errors_say_what_next", "label": "Errors say what to do next", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'no config file found (looked in ...). Run \"ddrop init\" to create one.' beats a bare ENOENT."}, {"id": "contributing_no_secrets_in_logs", "label": "Nothing secret reaches a log", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The logger redacts by field name and value pattern, but redaction is a backstop, not a licence to log freely."}, {"id": "contributing_zero_runtime_dependencies", "label": "No dependencies without a strong reason", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The runtime holds credentials, so every dependency is supply-chain surface; the project has zero runtime dependencies outside its own packages and that is worth defending."}, {"id": "contributing_protocol_version", "label": "PROTOCOL_VERSION and wire compatibility", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 22", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The protocol is a wire contract between machines that may run different versions, so any change to the envelope, frame layout or error codes is a compatibility question first; bump PROTOCOL_VERSION and state how mixed-version peers behave."}, {"id": "contributing_sdk_additive_changes", "label": "Transport SDK changes are additive only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Packages outside this repository compile against it; a non-additive change needs a version bump and a migration note, and a new capability must gate its conformance tests so existing adapters keep passing."}, {"id": "contributing_transports_live_outside", "label": "Transports are published outside this repository", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Publish as <scope>/deaddrop-transport-<name>; transports living outside this repository is the design working, not a gap in it."}, {"id": "docs_writing_a_transport", "label": "docs/writing-a-transport.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "agents_invariant_transport_imports", "target": "contributing_zero_runtime_dependencies", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "CONTRIBUTING.md", "source_location": "line 18", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_invariant_sdk_only_publi